<caml:Description xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><caml:Id>20250AB__150699INT</caml:Id><caml:VersionNum>99</caml:VersionNum><caml:History><caml:Action><caml:ActionText>INTRODUCED</caml:ActionText><caml:ActionDate>2025-02-26</caml:ActionDate></caml:Action></caml:History><caml:LegislativeInfo><caml:SessionYear>2025</caml:SessionYear><caml:SessionNum>0</caml:SessionNum><caml:MeasureType>AB</caml:MeasureType><caml:MeasureNum>1506</caml:MeasureNum><caml:MeasureState>INT</caml:MeasureState></caml:LegislativeInfo><caml:AuthorText authorType="LEAD_AUTHOR">Introduced by Committee on Agriculture (Assembly Members Soria (Chair), Alanis (Vice Chair), Aguiar-Curry, Connolly, Jeff Gonzalez, Hadwick, Irwin, and Ransom)</caml:AuthorText><caml:Authors><caml:Committee><caml:Contribution>LEAD_AUTHOR</caml:Contribution><caml:House>ASSEMBLY</caml:House><caml:Name>Committee on Agriculture</caml:Name><caml:Members>Assembly Members Soria (Chair), Alanis (Vice Chair), Aguiar-Curry, Connolly, Jeff Gonzalez, Hadwick, Irwin, and Ransom</caml:Members></caml:Committee></caml:Authors><caml:Title> An act to amend Section 5261 of the Food and Agricultural Code, relating to pests. </caml:Title><caml:RelatingClause>pests</caml:RelatingClause><caml:GeneralSubject><caml:Subject>Invasive pests: lists.</caml:Subject></caml:GeneralSubject><caml:DigestText><p>Existing law requires the Department of Food and Agriculture to develop and maintain a list of invasive pests, as defined, that have a reasonable likelihood of entering California for which a detection, exclusion, eradication, control, or management action by the state might be appropriate.</p><p>This bill would require the department to post the list on its internet website.</p></caml:DigestText><caml:DigestKey><caml:VoteRequired>MAJORITY</caml:VoteRequired><caml:Appropriation>NO</caml:Appropriation><caml:FiscalCommittee>YES</caml:FiscalCommittee><caml:LocalProgram>NO</caml:LocalProgram></caml:DigestKey><caml:MeasureIndicators><caml:ImmediateEffect>NO</caml:ImmediateEffect><caml:ImmediateEffectFlags><caml:Urgency>NO</caml:Urgency><caml:TaxLevy>NO</caml:TaxLevy><caml:Election>NO</caml:Election><caml:UsualCurrentExpenses>NO</caml:UsualCurrentExpenses><caml:BudgetBill>NO</caml:BudgetBill><caml:Prop25TrailerBill>NO</caml:Prop25TrailerBill></caml:ImmediateEffectFlags></caml:MeasureIndicators></caml:Description><caml:Bill id="bill" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><caml:Preamble>The people of the State of California do enact as follows:</caml:Preamble><caml:BillSection id="id_F3DD41EC-B220-4F54-9D3F-25B2F51B32FB"><caml:Num>SECTION 1.</caml:Num><caml:ActionLine action="IS_AMENDED" xlink:type="locator" xlink:href="urn:caml:codes:FAC:caml#xpointer(%2Fcaml%3ALawDoc%2Fcaml%3ACode%2Fcaml%3ALawHeading%5B%40type%3D'DIVISION'%20and%20caml%3ANum%3D'4.'%5D%2Fcaml%3ALawHeading%5B%40type%3D'PART'%20and%20caml%3ANum%3D'1.'%5D%2Fcaml%3ALawHeading%5B%40type%3D'CHAPTER'%20and%20caml%3ANum%3D'4.5.'%5D%2Fcaml%3ALawSection%5Bcaml%3ANum%3D'5261.'%5D)" xlink:label="fractionType: LAW_SECTION">Section 5261 of the <caml:DocName>Food and Agricultural Code</caml:DocName> is amended to read:</caml:ActionLine><caml:Fragment><caml:LawSection id="id_3050443E-B6D6-4271-B67E-E0C6F85BEB5D"><caml:Num>5261.</caml:Num><caml:LawSectionVersion id="id_E4C5F11D-3C85-43D3-9E07-5AFFFB9CE3B4"><caml:Content><p>The department shall<?xm-deletion_mark data=" develop and maintain"?><?xm-insertion_mark_start?> develop, maintain, and post on its internet website<?xm-insertion_mark_end?> a list of invasive pests that have a reasonable likelihood of entering California for which a detection, exclusion, eradication, control, or management action by the state might be appropriate. In developing the list, the department shall consider any invasive pests identified by the federal or state government for which a detection, exclusion, eradication, control, or management action might be undertaken.</p></caml:Content></caml:LawSectionVersion></caml:LawSection></caml:Fragment></caml:BillSection></caml:Bill></caml:MeasureDoc>